Of course due to the doubling experience requirements, there are twice
as many miles from 15 to 16, twice more from 16 to 17, and so on to
level 22, where the experience needed to advance settles down to
"only" 10M more points between levels.

The most important levels, in my book, are 2 (desperately needed
sometimes), level 7 (the point where I begin to suspect a character
might be a keeper) and 14 (quest qualification).  People playing
normally rarely gain levels above 14 through experience gain alone,
and the color system would be practically useless after level 19,
where the red color from drinking an uncursed potion of raise level,
and the yellow from drinking a blessed one, is almost a meaningless
distinction.

The worst thing about this system, however, would be that it would
make a red-text HP color warning (such as implemented on
nethack.alt.org) less impressive.  When there's *always* something red
in the status line, it makes a red HP reading a lot less ominous.  Red
is a warning color, and if the player's experience total is red a
newbie player may get the impression that he's in danger every time he
levels.

Not trying to dump sand on the idea, it might be cool to have some
notification of impending leveling.  It'd certainly make the long road
to level 14 seem more bearable.

